# Build-context exclusions for docker/Dockerfile.
#
# With `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` BuildKit reads this file
# (`<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`), never docker/.dockerignore, so that file has
# never applied. This list keeps a LOCAL build's context the same as CI's clean
# checkout: it drops only what a fresh `git clone` would not contain. Without it
# a working tree sent agent worktrees (.claude/worktrees, ~35 GB with their own
# node_modules) and Docker Desktop's daemon ran out of memory mid-build
# (2026-10-23, the v5.27.0 release).

.git/
.claude/worktrees/
private/
data/
node_modules/
addons/*/node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
tests/e2e/.output/
tests/e2e/.auth/
**/.vitest-cache/
reports/
exports/
search-index/
*.log
